Title: The Forge
Credit: An Ikenga Studio piece
Draft date: 2026-07-15
Notes: Ember-noir. Six beats. A blacksmith gives life to an iron mask.

===

INT. THE WORKSHOP - NIGHT

A dim ironworking workshop at night. A glowing forge at the center of
the room. Hanging tools in silhouette against the dark. Embers drift
slowly in the air. Warm orange key light carves through deep shadow.
Cinematic, shallow depth of field.

The forge glows in the dark. Embers drift upward like slow stars. A
slow push-in toward the fire.

INT. THE WORKSHOP - NIGHT - THE ANVIL

ADAORA stands at the anvil, soot on her hands and forearms. She raises
the hammer high. Firelight carves her face out of the shadow.

She holds there, framed against the glow, steady and unhurried.

INT. THE WORKSHOP - NIGHT - THE MASK

Close on the anvil. An iron mask, half-formed, lies on the face of the
steel. Sparks catch along its edge as it turns beneath the hammer's
shadow. A slow tilt down the cheekplate. Embers.

INT. THE WORKSHOP - NIGHT - THE STRIKE

Adaora brings the hammer down. A single, heavy blow. Sparks erupt
outward in a bright fan. The workshop seems to hold its breath in the
flash.

INT. THE WORKSHOP - NIGHT - THE EYES

The iron mask's eyes catch the firelight's glow. For a moment nothing
moves. Then something behind the eyes stirs -- almost still, a flicker
of life that was not there before.

INT. THE WORKSHOP - NIGHT - ALIVE

Adaora steps back, hands falling to her sides. The glowing iron mask
lies between her hands and the fire -- alive now, breathing its own
heat. A slow pull-back into the dark of the workshop.

THE END
